# Wave H.n — Operator admin DOM attrs

## Problem

After H.l / H.l.b, `apps/web` still hosted dozens of **`data-denali-*`** hooks on platform admin chrome:

- dashboard widgets / KPI / registration rows
- page header, empty state, skeleton, confirm dialog
- welcome dialog, profile avatar, finance board tabs
- motion: `data-denali-animate` / `data-denali-animate-delay`

These are **operator shell** contracts, not Denali product fields — yet Denali theme CSS keyed off the product prefix, so every workspace skin path still looked Denali-branded in the DOM.

## Decision

1. Replace every `data-denali-` **attribute name prefix** with `data-operator-` in:
   - `apps/web/{src,app,test,tests,scripts}`
   - `packages/workspaces/denali/theme/*.css`
   - `packages/workspaces/denali/src/**` emitters of the same attrs
2. Keep broader Denali **BEM** (`.denali-wizard-composite`, pickers, …) for later; datetime/date-picker BEM → [`wave-h-operator-datetime-bem.mdoc`](./wave-h-operator-datetime-bem.mdoc) (Wave H.p). This wave is **data-attribute** neutralization only.
3. Specs that assert `[data-denali-animate=…]` / confirm-dialog attrs must target `data-operator-*`.

## Out of scope

- Renaming `CreateTourWizardDenaliHeader` / draft `resolveDenali*` shell helpers → [`wave-h-operator-shell-ts-names.mdoc`](./wave-h-operator-shell-ts-names.mdoc) (Wave H.o)
- Removing `apps/web/src/wizard/denali/*` firewall
- Install-graph isolation
- Broader wizard BEM (composite / review / pickers); datetime BEM done in H.p

## Verify

```bash
rg 'data-denali-' apps/web/src apps/web/app --glob '!**/*.generated.*'
# expect empty
rg 'data-denali-' packages/workspaces/denali/theme --glob '*.css'
# expect empty
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-h-operator-admin-dom.spec.ts \
  test/denali-admin-theme.spec.ts \
  test/denali-confirm-dialog.spec.ts
```
